# Portfolio UI Rules

Follow `.agents/skills/design-taste-frontend` (Taste Skill). Site-specific constraints:

## Design dials

- `DESIGN_VARIANCE: 6`
- `MOTION_INTENSITY: 7`
- `VISUAL_DENSITY: 4`

## Layout

- One primary section per viewport (`min-h-dvh` + scroll snap).
- Hero is full-bleed video background. No cards in the hero.
- Hero budget: brand name, one headline, one supporting sentence, one CTA group.
- One job per section. Do not repeat skills/projects content across sections.
- Keep Ubuntu as the UI typeface. Giant footer wordmark uses EB Garamond (`--font-garamond`), uppercase, dull metallic - not neon. Avoid Inter/Roboto/Arial defaults.

## Motion

- Use GSAP + ScrollTrigger for section choreography.
- Do not mix GSAP and Motion/framer-motion in the same component tree.
- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion`.

## Visual direction

- No purple-on-white / purple-indigo mesh defaults.
- No warm cream + terracotta + serif newspaper look.
- No hero overlays (floating badges, promo chips on media).
- Atmosphere via video, gradients, or subtle texture. Not flat single-color pages only.
